Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||11-27-2000||10:16 PM||||Well that was a waste of time.. I took an hour to go vote today, had to register because I just moved here in august and wasn't on the voter list, and when I finally got the ballot... the party I prefer wasn't even represented!<P>I had a choice of:<P>Liberal (best choice of those available..)<BR>Canadian Alliance (no thanks.)<BR>NDP (LOL..)<BR>Communist (riiiight.......)<P>Honestly, I prefer the "popular vote" system the Americans use.. I think it needs to be updated though, punching holes in a piece of paper etc is ridiculous. computers are reliable enough to handle bank transactions every day.. running flight schedules.. running nuclear plants.. so why can't a computerized voting system be implemented? the cost savings of printing up ballots, paying to have them counted, etc. should EASILY cover the costs of making the voting units..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||13
